backend-1   | ╭─────────────────────────── ✅ Agent Final Answer ────────────────────────────╮
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  Agent: Schema Analysis Specialist                                           │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  Final Answer:                                                               │
backend-1   | │  **Answer**                                                                  │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  Below is the concrete “minimal‑sufficient” model that can answer the        │
backend-1   | │  question                                                                    │
backend-1   | │  **“إجمالي إيرادات الأفلام وعدد المشاهدات حسب التصنيف العمري وتصنيف          │
backend-1   | │  الأفلام”**                                                                  │
backend-1   | │  ( total movie revenue + total view count, grouped by *age rating* and       │
backend-1   | │  *film genre* ).                                                             │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ---                                                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ### 1️⃣ Tables that must be involved                                         │
backend-1   | │  | # | Table | Why it is needed |                                            │
backend-1   | │  |---|-------|------------------|                                            │
backend-1   | │  | 1 | `dev_film` | Holds the film master record, including the              │
backend-1   | │  **age‑rating** column (`rating`). |                                         │
backend-1   | │  | 2 | `dev_film_category` | Bridge (many‑to‑many) table that links a film   │
backend-1   | │  to one or more categories (genres). |                                       │
backend-1   | │  | 3 | `dev_category` | Stores the **genre name** (`name`). |                │
backend-1   | │  | 4 | `dev_inventory` | Connects a physical copy of a film (`film_id`) to   │
backend-1   | │  a store; needed to reach rentals/payments. |                                │
backend-1   | │  | 5 | `dev_rental` | One row per “view” (rental) → gives the **view         │
backend-1   | │  count**. Contains `rental_id` and `inventory_id`. |                         │
backend-1   | │  | 6 | `dev_payment` (or its monthly partitions `dev_payment_p2022_XX`) |    │
backend-1   | │  Holds the **payment amount** for each rental → source of revenue            │
backend-1   | │  (`amount`). Contains `rental_id`. |                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  > **Note** – If you are using the partitioned payment tables, query them    │
backend-1   | │  together (e.g., `UNION ALL`) or use the base view `dev_payment` if it       │
backend-1   | │  already abstracts the partitions.                                           │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ---                                                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ### 2️⃣ Join path (logic)                                                    │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ```                                                                         │
backend-1   | │  dev_film                                                                    │
backend-1   | │     ──► rating               (age‑rating column, no join needed)             │
backend-1   | │     │                                                                        │
backend-1   | │     └─► film_id                                                              │
backend-1   | │          └─► dev_film_category.film_id                                       │
backend-1   | │                  └─► dev_category.category_id   → category.name   (genre)    │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  dev_film.film_id                                                            │
backend-1   | │     └─► dev_inventory.film_id                                                │
backend-1   | │              └─► dev_rental.inventory_id                                     │
backend-1   | │                      └─► dev_payment.rental_id                               │
backend-1   | │  ```                                                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  **Explanation of the path**                                                 │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  1. **Film → Genre**                                                         │
backend-1   | │     * `dev_film_category` is the many‑to‑many bridge that maps each          │
backend-1   | │  `film_id` to one or more `category_id`.                                     │
backend-1   | │     * `dev_category` supplies the human‑readable genre (`name`).             │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  2. **Film → Revenue / View count**                                          │
backend-1   | │     * From a film we reach its physical copies via `dev_inventory`.          │
backend-1   | │     * Each inventory item that has been rented appears in `dev_rental`. The  │
backend-1   | │  number of rows per film = **view count**.                                   │
backend-1   | │     * Every rental that generated money appears in `dev_payment` (or its     │
backend-1   | │  monthly shards). Summing `amount` per film yields **total revenue**.        │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  3. **Aggregation**                                                          │
backend-1   | │     * After the joins, group by `dev_film.rating` (age rating) **and**       │
backend-1   | │  `dev_category.name` (genre).                                                │
backend-1   | │     * Compute `SUM(dev_payment.amount)` → total revenue.                     │
backend-1   | │     * Compute `COUNT(DISTINCT dev_rental.rental_id)` (or `COUNT(*)` on       │
backend-1   | │  rental rows) → total view count.                                            │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ---                                                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ### 3️⃣ Required columns (per table)                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  | Table | Columns needed for the query |                                    │
backend-1   | │  |-------|------------------------------|                                    │
backend-1   | │  | **dev_film** | `film_id` (PK), `rating` (age‑rating) |                    │
backend-1   | │  | **dev_film_category** | `film_id`, `category_id` |                        │
backend-1   | │  | **dev_category** | `category_id` (PK), `name` (genre) |                   │
backend-1   | │  | **dev_inventory** | `inventory_id` (PK), `film_id` |                      │
backend-1   | │  | **dev_rental** | `rental_id` (PK), `inventory_id` |                       │
backend-1   | │  | **dev_payment** (or each partition) | `payment_id` (PK), `rental_id`,     │
backend-1   | │  `amount` |                                                                  │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  *Only the columns listed above are required; any additional columns can be  │
backend-1   | │  ignored.*                                                                   │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ---                                                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ### 4️⃣ Sketch of the final SQL (illustrative)                               │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ```sql                                                                      │
backend-1   | │  SELECT                                                                      │
backend-1   | │      f.rating          AS age_rating,                                        │
backend-1   | │      c.name            AS genre,                                             │
backend-1   | │      COUNT(DISTINCT r.rental_id)          AS total_views,                    │
backend-1   | │      SUM(p.amount)                        AS total_revenue                   │
backend-1   | │  FROM dev_film               AS f                                            │
backend-1   | │  JOIN dev_film_category      AS fc  ON fc.film_id      = f.film_id           │
backend-1   | │  JOIN dev_category           AS c   ON c.category_id   = fc.category_id      │
backend-1   | │  JOIN dev_inventory          AS i   ON i.film_id       = f.film_id           │
backend-1   | │  JOIN dev_rental             AS r   ON r.inventory_id  = i.inventory_id      │
backend-1   | │  JOIN dev_payment            AS p   ON p.rental_id     = r.rental_id         │
backend-1   | │  GROUP BY                                                                    │
backend-1   | │      f.rating,                                                               │
backend-1   | │      c.name                                                                  │
backend-1   | │  ORDER BY                                                                    │
backend-1   | │      f.rating,                                                               │
backend-1   | │      c.name;                                                                 │
backend-1   | │  ```                                                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  *(If you need to read the monthly shards, replace `dev_payment` with a      │
backend-1   | │  `UNION ALL` of the `dev_payment_p2022_XX` tables.)*                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  ---                                                                         │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
