backend-1   | │  `rental_id`            |                                                    │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  **Explanation**                                                             │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_film.film_id` is the primary identifier for a film.                  │
backend-1   | │    * It links to `dev_film_category.film_id` (many‑to‑many bridge to         │
backend-1   | │  genres).                                                                    │
backend-1   | │    * It also links to `dev_inventory.film_id` (physical copies of the        │
backend-1   | │  film).                                                                      │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_film_category.category_id` joins to `dev_category.category_id` to    │
backend-1   | │  obtain the genre name.                                                      │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_inventory.inventory_id` joins to `dev_rental.inventory_id` – each    │
backend-1   | │  rental (view) references the inventory item that was rented.                │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  * `dev_rental.rental_id` joins to `dev_payment.rental_id` – each payment    │
backend-1   | │  is tied to the rental that generated it.                                    │
backend-1   | │                                                                              │
backend-1   | │  These relationships form a complete path from the **fact** (payments &      │
backend-1   | │  rentals) to the **dimensions** (film age rating and genre), enabling the    │
